# The archive's work in the media pool that takes the media worker's CPU budget, a kind a line, in
# the order offered. `reserve` puts a kind in the share kept for the work after ingest
# (CFG_CPU_NON_ENTRY_SLOTS). Every kind a pipeline step names with `requires: cpu` is here, or it
# never runs (test/media/model-slots.test.ts).
#
# Some run on EiN's own data:
unzip                    # a zip in a staging category expanded                (priority 100)
interpret reserve        # what a file's metadata means: its time and place    (priority 100)
face-assign reserve      # a kNN over every known face embedding               (priority 40)
speaker-assign reserve   # the same for a recording's voices                   (priority 40)
dedupe reserve           # a staged file's duplicate findings                  (priority 20)
retime reserve           # staged files dated by a category's rules            (priority 20)
organize reserve         # a staging category's groups planned again           (priority 15)
sidecars reserve         # Takeout and XMP sidecars paired with files          (priority 30)
# and one waits on EMS, which decodes the media:
fingerprint reserve      # perceptual hashes                                   (priority 30)
